{"info": {"author": null, "author_email": "Chad Smith <chadsmith.software@gmail.com>", "bugtrack_url": null, "classifiers": ["Operating System :: OS Independent", "Programming Language :: Python", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3 :: Only", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.12", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.13", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.14", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.15"], "description": "<p align=\"center\">\n<a href=\"https://pipx.pypa.io\">\n<img align=\"center\" src=\"https://github.com/pypa/pipx/raw/main/logo.svg\" width=\"200\"/>\n</a>\n</p>\n\n# pipx \u2014 Install and Run Python Applications in Isolated Environments\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n<a href=\"https://github.com/pypa/pipx/raw/main/pipx_demo.gif\">\n<img src=\"https://github.com/pypa/pipx/raw/main/pipx_demo.gif\"/>\n</a>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n<a href=\"https://github.com/pypa/pipx/actions/workflows/tests.yml\">\n<img src=\"https://github.com/pypa/pipx/actions/workflows/tests.yml/badge.svg?event=push&branch=main\" alt=\"image\" /></a> <a href=\"https://badge.fury.io/py/pipx\"><img src=\"https://badge.fury.io/py/pipx.svg\" alt=\"PyPI version\"></a> <a href=\"https://badge.fury.io/py/pipx\"><img src=\"https://static.pepy.tech/badge/pipx\"></a>\n<a href=\"https://scorecard.dev/viewer/?uri=github.com/pypa/pipx\"><img src=\"https://api.scorecard.dev/projects/github.com/pypa/pipx/badge\" alt=\"OpenSSF Scorecard\"></a>\n<a href=\"https://www.bestpractices.dev/projects/16273\"><img src=\"https://www.bestpractices.dev/projects/16273/badge\" alt=\"OpenSSF Best Practices\"></a>\n\n</p>\n\n**Documentation**: <https://pipx.pypa.io>\n\n**Source Code**: <https://github.com/pypa/pipx>\n\n_For comparison to other tools including [pipsi](https://github.com/mitsuhiko/pipsi), see\n[Comparison to Other Tools](https://pipx.pypa.io/stable/explanation/comparisons.html)._\n\n## Overview: What is `pipx`?\n\npipx installs and runs end-user applications written in Python. It's roughly similar to macOS's [brew](https://brew.sh),\nJavaScript's [npx](https://medium.com/@maybekatz/introducing-npx-an-npm-package-runner-55f7d4bd282b), and Linux's\n[apt](https://wiki.debian.org/Apt).\n\nIt's closely related to [pip](https://pip.pypa.io). It installs with [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) when available and\n`pip` otherwise, but focuses on installing and managing Python packages you run directly from the command line as\napplications.\n\n### Features\n\n`pipx` enables you to\n\n- expose CLI entrypoints of packages (\"apps\") installed to isolated environments with the `install` command,\n    guaranteeing no dependency conflicts and clean uninstalls;\n- list, upgrade, and uninstall packages you installed with pipx; and\n- run the latest version of a Python application in a temporary environment with the `run` command.\n\npipx runs with regular user permissions and never calls `sudo pip install`.\n\n## Install pipx\n\n### On macOS\n\n```\nbrew install pipx\npipx ensurepath\n```\n\n### On Linux\n\nInstall pipx with your distribution's package manager. See the\n[Linux installation instructions](https://pipx.pypa.io/stable/how-to/install-pipx.html) for commands and alternatives.\n\n```\npipx ensurepath\n```\n\n### On Windows\n\n```\nscoop install pipx\npipx ensurepath\n```\n\nFor more detailed installation instructions, see the\n[full documentation](https://pipx.pypa.io/stable/how-to/install-pipx.html).\n\n## Quick Start\n\nInstall an application for your user:\n\n```\npipx install pycowsay\npycowsay mooo\n```\n\nRun an application without installing:\n\n```\npipx run pycowsay moo\n```\n\nSee the [full documentation](https://pipx.pypa.io/stable/) for more details.\n\n## Contributing\n\nIssues and pull requests are welcome. Check out [Contributing](https://pipx.pypa.io/stable/contributing.html) to get\nstarted. We expect everyone who interacts with the pipx project via codebase, issue tracker, chat rooms, or otherwise to\nfollow the [PSF Code of Conduct](https://github.com/pypa/.github/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).\n", "description_content_type": "text/markdown", "docs_url": null, "download_url": null, "downloads": {"last_day": -1, "last_month": -1, "last_week": -1}, "dynamic": null, "home_page": null, "keywords": "Virtual Environment, cli, install, pip, workflow", "license": null, "license_expression": "MIT", "license_files": ["LICENSE"], "maintainer": null, "maintainer_email": null, "name": "pipx", "package_url": "https://pypi.org/project/pipx/", "platform": null, "project_url": "https://pypi.org/project/pipx/", "project_urls": {"Changelog": "https://pipx.pypa.io/latest/changelog.html", "Documentation": "https://pipx.pypa.io", "Homepage": "https://pipx.pypa.io", "Issue Tracker": "https://github.com/pypa/pipx/issues", "Source Code": "https://github.com/pypa/pipx"}, "provides_extra": ["uv"], "release_url": "https://pypi.org/project/pipx/1.18.19/", "requires_dist": ["argcomplete>=3.7.2", "colorama>=0.4.6; sys_platform == \"win32\"", "filelock>=4.2", "packaging>=26.3", "platformdirs>=4.12.2", "userpath!=1.9,>=1.9.2", "uv>=0.12.22; extra == \"uv\""], "requires_python": ">=3.11", "summary": "Install and Run Python Applications in Isolated Environments", "version": "1.18.19", "yanked": false, "yanked_reason": null}, "release_dates": {"0.1.0": "2017-07-27T01:47:23.213987Z", "0.1.1": "2017-07-27T02:05:11.275087Z", "0.12.0.0": "2019-02-06T05:11:59.489410Z", "0.12.0.1": "2019-02-08T01:46:42.030368Z", "0.12.0.2": "2019-02-09T17:58:49.333487Z", "0.12.0.3": "2019-02-09T18:34:58.288042Z", "0.12.0.4": "2019-02-09T18:57:04.926974Z", "0.12.1.0": "2019-02-14T17:02:46.922902Z", "0.12.2.0": "2019-02-19T05:14:51.207533Z", "0.12.3.0": "2019-02-23T20:46:14.472640Z", "0.12.3.1": "2019-02-25T16:54:15.114798Z", "0.12.3.2": "2019-03-07T17:16:46.224454Z", "0.12.3.3": "2019-03-08T01:07:41.505992Z", "0.13.0.0": "2019-04-06T00:52:34.938986Z", "0.13.0.0b1": "2019-04-06T00:36:02.515462Z", "0.13.0.1": "2019-04-0